; Regression (2026-09-23): the planner registered `aligned_alloc` as a built-in
; C runtime function, although the runtime has called scaly_aligned_alloc for
; a long time and nothing called the bare name. Any program could call it with
; no declaration and it was emitted against a synthesized `(...)` signature,
; rc 0 — on a target whose libc has no aligned_alloc (MSVC) that is a link
; failure with no line and no relation to the change that caused it.
; xfail: error: function not found: aligned_alloc
let p aligned_alloc(16, 64)
if p <> null
    print("PASS")
